She looked fine. Her cro­cus dress she wore low­cut, be­long­ings on show. Clove her breath was al­ways in theatre when she bent to ask a ques­tion. Told her what Spinoza says in that book of poor papa’s. Hyp­not­ised, listen­ing. Eyes like that. She bent. Chap in dress­circle star­ing down in­to her with his op­era­glass for all he was worth. Beauty of mu­sic you must hear twice. Nature wo­man half a look. God made the coun­try man the tune. Met him pike hoses. Philo­sophy. O rocks!

